   "summary": "Seyi Tinubu, son of President Bola Tinubu, has sparked reactions online after a viral video showed him handing a bundle of cash to a female passenger in a commercial tricycle during a political mobilisation visit to Kebbi State. The woman had just expressed support for President Tinubu when Seyi handed her the money.",
   "summary_zh": "总统博拉·蒂努布之子塞伊·蒂努布在网络上引发热议。一段广泛传播的视频显示，他到凯贝比州进行政治动员访问时，将一捆现金递给一名乘坐商用三轮车的女乘客。就在塞伊给这名女子钱之前，她刚刚表示支持蒂努布总统。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Seyi Tinubu, son of President Bola Tinubu, has sparked reactions online after a viral video showed him handing a bundle of cash to a female passenger in a commercial tricycle during a political mobilisation visit to Kebbi State. The woman had just expressed support for President Tinubu when Seyi handed her the money. Reps threaten action as ministers shun research fund hearing NUC approves new private university in Osun Join me in Rainbow Coalition or leave, Fubara tells supporters The incident has triggered debate about political generosity, voter influence and possible vote-buying ahead of the 2027 general elections. Although the video does not establish that the money was exchanged for a promise to vote, questions are being raised about whether political support should be earned through policies and performance rather than cash handouts. Our Reporters",
