   "title": "Putin open to Europe joining Ukraine peace talks, says Witkoff",
   "url": "https://www.politico.eu/article/vladimir-putin-open-to-europe-joining-ukraine-peace-talks-steve-witkoff/",
   "domain": "politico.eu",
   "source": "politico.eu",
   "published": "Thu, 12 Nov 2026 20:10:38 +0000",
   "_dt": 1794514238.0,
   "ageDays": 0.04,
   "summary": "DUBLIN— Russian President Vladimir Putin agreed Thursday to allow European representatives to join the next round of peace talks on Ukraine, U.S. presidential special envoy Steve Witkoff said . “The Europeans will join at the next meeting, which we think is a very big deal, because it’s important, they are our partners and it’s important for them to be involved, ” he said, speaking alongside fellow U.S. envoy Jared Kushner after a four-and-a-half-hour meeting with Putin in Moscow.",
   "summary_zh": "都柏林——美国总统特使史蒂夫·维特科夫周四表示，俄罗斯总统弗拉基米尔·普京已同意让欧洲方面的代表参加下一轮乌克兰和平会谈。“欧洲人将参加下一次会议，我们认为这意义重大，因为这很重要，他们是我们的伙伴，让他们参与进来很重要。”他说。他是在莫斯科与普京会面四个半小时后，与美国特使贾里德·库什纳一同出席活动时说这番话的。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "DUBLIN— Russian President Vladimir Putin agreed Thursday to allow European representatives to join the next round of peace talks on Ukraine, U.S. presidential special envoy Steve Witkoff said . “The Europeans will join at the next meeting, which we think is a very big deal, because it’s important, they are our partners and it’s important for them to be involved, ” he said, speaking alongside fellow U.S. envoy Jared Kushner after a four-and-a-half-hour meeting with Putin in Moscow. The EU has long been pushing for a seat at the negotiating table. The two U.S. envoys are meeting Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy late Thursday in Dublin, where he attended a meeting of the European Political Community and where EU leaders will discuss the Ukraine peace talks on Friday. In Dublin, we “will download Zelenskyy on everything that has occurred,” Witkoff said. European governments so far have been skeptical about the prospects for a breakthrough following the latest round of talks in Abu Dhabi this week. “The Russian demands are the same maximalist demands that we have heard for years,” said a diplomat, who was granted anonymity because the discussions were confidential. Two officials from the EU, Björn Seibert, chief of staff to Commission President Ursula von der Leyen, and Anna-Maria Boura, chief foreign policy adviser to European Council President António Costa , returned from Abu Dhabi and briefed EU ambassadors",
