   "summary": "As renewed diplomatic efforts seek to bring an end to Russia's war on Ukraine, the prospect of a negotiated settlement remains unlikely due to Russia's irreconcilable territorial demands, competing visions of European security and an increasingly unpredictable and pro-Moscow American approach to mediation.",
   "summary_zh": "尽管各方再次开展外交努力，试图结束俄罗斯对乌克兰的战争，但由于俄罗斯提出无法调和的领土要求、各方对欧洲安全存在不同构想，以及美国在调解问题上采取越来越难以预测且亲莫斯科的立场，通过谈判达成解决方案的可能性依然不大。",
   "summarySource": "index",
   "body": "As renewed diplomatic efforts seek to bring an end to Russia's war on Ukraine, the prospect of a negotiated settlement remains unlikely due to Russia's irreconcilable territorial demands, competing visions of European security and an increasingly unpredictable and pro-Moscow American approach to mediation. For Russia expert Mark Galeotti, Executive Director of Mayak Intelligence and Honorary Professor at University College London's School of Slavonic and East European Studies, Moscow's maximalist vision conceals a more complex negotiating strategy. \"The Russian approach is always to sound incredibly bullish and then make any concessions at the very last minute,\" he explains, suggesting that the Kremlin's uncompromising rhetoric should not necessarily be mistaken for an absolute refusal to negotiate. Yet the territorial dispute over Donbas presents a particularly formidable obstacle. Puti",
